  "details": "Meta Quest 2 Headset, gamepad (PS4 controller).\n\nUpon booting VRChat for the first time on the newest open beta build, a black screen is placed directly in front of my view. This was observed when downloading or switching worlds. Some effects were able to pass through this screen (similar to a screenshot taken by @.uasset on Discord, 1st image attached). \n\nThe object was also loaded within the physical world I joined (2nd image). It respawns whenever I open my menu or enter a world. Its visibility appears to ignore objects placed in front of it (example in the 3rd image). \n\nUnfortunately, this bug only appeared in my first session of this build. I attempted to recreate the bug by opening VRChat 5 more times, but it no longer appears. These trials were run side-by-side without turning off the headset. The browser application was opened during the first appearance in image #2. \n\nThis bug only appears locally and is not visible to other users.\n\nTimeline of events:\n\n1: Download build #1744 of VRChat open beta. \n\n2: Open/boot up VRChat.\n\n3: Black screen object appears while downloading Home World.\n\n4: Black screen object appears in the direction of view within my home World.\n\n5: Opening the launch pad at any time respawns the black screen object.\n\n6: Attempt to join friends.\n\n7: Black screen object still appears within the loading screen.\n\n8: Black screen object still appears in view in the world.\n\n9: Black screen object still respawns when opening the menu.\n\n10: I close the VRChat application and upload my screenshots to Discord.\n\n11: I attempt to recreate the bug 5 more times.",
